kind Required Common optional Notes <code>Agent</code> <code>image</code> <code>framework</code>, <code>protocol</code> (<code>mcp/a2a/openapi/http/custom</code>), <code>agent_card_url</code> (A2A card, required when protocol=a2a), <code>capabilities[]</code>, <code>env[]</code> env entry: <code>{name, value}</code> or <code>{name, value_from: {secret_ref: {name, key}}}</code>; cluster placement (namespace/replicas) belongs to the Deployment <code>MCPServer</code> <code>transport</code> + (<code>endpoint</code> or <code>command</code>) <code>args[]</code> (stdio only, e.g. the args of <code>npx -y @mcp/xxx</code>), <code>headers[]</code> (remote auth headers, same shape as env entries, values may reference Secrets), <code>env[]</code> transport ∈ <code>streamable-http / sse / stdio</code>; http kinds require endpoint, stdio requires command and forbids args <code>Skill</code> <code>source.git.url</code> or <code>instructions</code> (either) <code>entrypoint</code>, <code>source.git.ref/subdirectory/credentials_ref</code> see git-source section <code>Prompt</code> <code>template</code> <code>variables[]</code> (<code>{name, required, description}</code>) project-private; every <code>{{placeholder}}</code> in the template must be declared — and every declared variable used — or publishing is rejected <p>Declared variables power structured forms in the console and structured MCP consumption:</p> <pre><code>kind: Prompt
metadata: {name: review-checklist, namespace: payment}
spec:
  template: "Review this change, focus on {{concerns}}"
  variables:
    - {name: concerns, required: true, description: risk areas to focus on}
    - {name: code, description: the code}
</code></pre> <p>| <code>Secret</code> | <code>data</code> (key/value object) | — | values envelope-encrypted, never returned; always <code>restricted</code> | | <code>Deployment</code> | <code>target_kind/target_namespace/target_name</code> | <code>tag</code> (pin), <code>cluster_namespace</code>, <code>replicas</code>, <code>port</code>, <code>image_pull_policy</code> | see Deploy to Kubernetes |</p>
